# Compiled C on SPARC64: the functions of sparc_compiled.c (shifts and logic,
# multiply and divide through %y, sign/zero-extending loads and narrow
# stores, float<->int conversion, float arithmetic, float compare-and-branch
# or conditional move, integer conditional move or branch, and a switch
# lowered to compares), compiled with clang -O2 for sparcv9-linux-gnu.
# Each optimized function should compute what the C source says.
# (This case found two remill bugs: `sdiv` divided by the zero-extended low
# word of its operand (Ghidra spec, now patched), so `mul_div` was wrong for
# negative divisors; and the `movl` in the delay slot of `retl` in
# `float_less` skipped the return on the path that moved, as p-code blocks
# ending at a local label left the instruction instead of falling through.)
#   tests/golden/tools/assemble.py --no-link --triple sparcv9-linux-gnu \
#       tests/golden/lifter/arch/sparc_compiled.c
